    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI can indeed reproduce the issue, however the solution is not quite right. Usually if there is a problem with some event not triggering, two most probable causes are: 1) it is executed inside an autocommand without `nested = true`; 2) there is an explicit/intentional 'eventignore'. The first one is the culprit in this case, as `nvim_buf_delete()` is executed inside a callback (`H.track_dir_edit`) for `BufEnter` function. Modifying the autocommand creation to include `nested = true` fixes the issue here.\r\n\r\nAlso note, that merging this will have to wait until 0.18.0 release.",
            "created_at": "2026-06-17T08:40:48Z",
